"""Authored claim map, serialized incrementally; no classification algorithm."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,csv
W=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
T1='MPL_137_002-044_transcription.tex'; T2='MPL_137_045-086_transcription.tex'
C=[]
canonical={int(r['entry_id'].split('#')[1]):r['item_id'] for r in csv.DictReader(W.joinpath('entries.tsv').open(),delimiter='\t')}
def add(n,items,scans,lines,words,statement,status,comp,cls,fate,dates,present,refs,confidence='high'):
    C.append(dict(id=f'CL-SA09-137-{n:03}',items=list(dict.fromkeys(canonical[i] for i in items)),cote='137',scans=scans,lines=lines,his_statement=words,statement=statement,status_on_pages=status,computation=comp,**{'class':('C' if n in (31,47) else cls)},fate=fate,fate_date=dates,present_status='As of November 2026: '+present,refs=refs,confidence=confidence))
    W.joinpath('claims.json').write_text(json.dumps(C,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))

add(1,[],[2],T1+':6-35','composantes projectives; π_i=0','For a nonnegative chain complex of projective k-modules with all homology zero, successive splittings decompose it into identity disks D_i(P_i), hence it is projective in Ch≥0(k). With H₀ projective and H_i=0 for i>0, add S₀(H₀). The interpretation of the damaged opening is reconstructed from the proof.','proved there','proof_audit.md §1 gives the degree-zero induction and the Hom characterization of projective disks.','E','Search S137-01/09: Dold–Puppe1961 §3 supplies the equivalence; the module splitting argument is elementary homological algebra already available before the catalogue date. The exact damaged opening is not independently restored.','Dold–Puppe announcement 1958 (identified from the 1961 bibliography); full paper 1961; manuscript catalogue 1975/76.','Valid with the stated nonnegative and projectivity hypotheses; no assertion for arbitrary two-sided acyclic projective complexes.',['DoldPuppe1961','StacksDK'])
add(2,[],[2],T1+':37-40','Γ^iΦ ⊗ Λ^jΨ; Λ^iΦ ⊗ Λ^jΨ','For i>0 and j≥0, the displayed simplicial modules are projective objects: the reduced functor Γ^i or Λ^i preserves the simplicial contraction of Φ, the remaining tensor factor has projective components, and normalization is nonnegative acyclic with projective components.','proof sketched','proof_audit.md §1; no numerical computation is needed.','E','Search S137-01: Dold–Puppe1961 §§1-3 give simplicial homotopy and the generalized Eilenberg–Zilber comparison. Combined with CL-SA09-137-001, they justify the stated scope. This does not say arbitrary nonlinear powers preserve projective homology.','1958 announcement;1961 publication.','Valid for these contractible generators and i>0.',['DoldPuppe1961','StacksDK'])
add(3,[],[4],T1+':83-111','(projectif) [flasque deleted]; q≥q′≥0; Hom(...)=0','The inserted projective-only hypothesis would imply Hom(L⊗Λ^qΨ,Λ^{q′}Ψ⊗M)=0 for q≥q′. It is false at q=q′: take k=Z, L=S₀(Z), q=q′=1 and M=Z. L is projective; both source and target are Ψ and identity is nonzero. Corrected statement: q′<q by support; equality additionally needs H_q of the source to vanish, e.g. acyclic L.','false as stated','proof_audit.md §1 checks every counterexample hypothesis and the corrected chain-map argument; no code required.','C','Search S137-01/09: normalization in Dold–Puppe §3 and Stacks019D identifies the missing homology condition. No literature theorem with the literal enlarged hypothesis can hold. The original flasque version is standard; uncertainty of the inserted word remains a scan issue.','Standard corrected argument predates1975/76; this explicit audit2026.','Refuted literal reading; corrected statement identified within this same claim, CL-SA09-137-003(corrected).',['DoldPuppe1961','StacksDK'])
add(4,[27,28,29],[4,73,74],T1+':113-130; '+T2+':998-1002','Il existe un homomorphisme de complexes; jusqu’au degré n incl.','For weight n, the complex Γ^{n-i}Φ⊗Λ^iΨ is compared to the exterior universal resolution; its last term identifies with the corresponding kernel. Evaluating a suitable additive functor is later asserted to give a homotopy equivalence with an upper truncation of F(C•), inducing cohomology isomorphisms through n. Good truncation, the exact resolution category, and compatibility with PD/multiplication are reconstruction requirements, not settled notation.','stated without proof','outputs/recompute.json: truncation_disk checks good versus brutal truncation; proof_audit.md §6. The whole weight-n comparison is not certified by this small test.','C','Search S137-01/06/11: Dold–Puppe and SGA4 XVII5.5 provide nonlinear derived-functor tools; Sullivan1977 §10 concerns rational models. No opened source proves the exact universal integral, weightwise, naturally compatible comparison as worded here. Modern reconstruction results have different enhancement hypotheses.','Dold–Puppe1961; SGA4 volume3 1973; Sullivan1977; exact manuscript identification remains unresolved2026.','The local additive comparison is plausible after specifying truncation and resolutions; the full structured assertion is not established by the sources searched.',['DoldPuppe1961','SGA4XVII','Sullivan1977','Horel2024'],'medium')
add(5,[],[7,8,9],T1+':178-305','somme directe ... Φ^i⊗M_i ... Ψ^j⊗N_j','A nonnegative normalized complex whose terms and homology are projective splits as ⊕_{i≥1}D_i(M_i)⊕⊕_{j≥0}S_j(N_j). Finite generation degreewise is equivalent to finite generation of the coefficient modules in each degree. The splitting is not canonical, though boundary and homology modules are intrinsic.','proved there','proof_audit.md §1 gives induction.','E','Search S137-01/09: Dold–Puppe§3 and the direct splitting argument identify this as classical decomposition under projective-homology hypotheses. PID classification in Rasmussen–Marchand §3.3 is a different, more general torsion variant.','Dold–Puppe1961; standard splitting predates the manuscript; modern explicit lecture treatment2019.','Valid; no replacement of projective coefficient modules by ranks over a general base.',['DoldPuppe1961','RasmussenMarchand2019'])
add(6,[],[7,9,11,13],T1+':178-221;272-305;352-366;436-460','ρ(n)=Σ μ_i binom(n+1,i)+Σ ν_j binom(n,j)','Over a nonzero connected commutative base with finite-projective terms and homology, the simplicial rank has this binomial expansion. Bounded polynomial growth is equivalent to bounded normalized support and hence finitely many nonzero disks/spheres. The sphere index includes0; leading coefficient in degree N is (μ_N+ν_N)/N!.','proof sketched','outputs/recompute.json: DK_rank, leading_term_degree3, Euler_at_minus_one. proof_audit.md §1 proves positivity and Pascal identity.','E','Search S137-01/09: Dold–Puppe1961 §3 formula(3.3) and Stacks019D’s inverse sum over surjections give the binomial rank formula. The margin omitting N! and one j≥1 version are reading alarms.','1958/1961 Dold–Puppe; observed numerical defects audited2026.','Valid after the explicit j=0 and leading-coefficient corrections; the source formula itself is retained in readings.tsv.',['DoldPuppe1961','StacksDK'])
add(7,[],[10],T1+':313-337','le produit tensoriel ... est spécial','The degreewise tensor of simplicial special objects remains special: reduce to the disk/sphere generators, use Eilenberg–Zilber and Künneth for projective homology, and the product rank polynomial for bounded normalization. Strictly special objects are base changes of special integral free models; the integral tensor splits into free disks and spheres, proving strict tensor closure over every commutative base.','proof sketched','proof_audit.md §1: the integer-model/base-change argument checks strict freeness; rank multiplication and Dold–Kan bound normalization. No finite calculation substitutes for the general argument.','E','Search S137-01/11: Dold–Puppe1961 §2 is the generalized Eilenberg–Zilber theorem. The source itself reduces the strict case to Z (scan10,lines320-321); this base-change argument proves freeness without assuming that all projectives over k are free.','Eilenberg–Zilber1953 cited in Dold–Puppe; Dold–Puppe1961.','Both special and strictly special tensor closure hold with the source’s coefficient-module definitions; nonlinear powers are a separate withdrawn assertion.',['DoldPuppe1961'],'high')
add(8,[],[10,11,12],T1+':316-318;368-401','faux','The proposed preservation of special objects by Γ, Λ and symmetric operations is retracted. In particular Γ² of the simplicial realization of Z[1] has normalized complex Z --2--> Z in degrees2,1, hence nonprojective H₁=Z/2.','corrected by himself later','programs/recompute.py, outputs/recompute.json Gamma2_KZ1; proof_audit.md §3 derives the faces and proves higher normalized groups vanish.','E','Search S137-01/09/11: non-additive derived functors were already the subject of Dold–Puppe1961 §§4,10-12 and SGA4 XVII5.5. Their existence is compatible with this explicit torsion obstruction; the exact Γ² computation is redone here rather than asserted from a broad citation.','1958 announcement;1961 full theory; source retraction on10-12.','The withdrawal is mathematically justified; it must not be promoted to a surviving closure theorem.',['DoldPuppe1961','SGA4XVII'])
add(9,[],[12],T1+':403-430','ρ(n) ... π_i ... déterminent ... à isomorphisme près','Numerical ranks of coefficient modules do not classify special objects over a general connected base. Over R=Z[√−5], R and the invertible ideal I=(2,1+√−5) both have rank1, but their constant simplicial modules are not isomorphic. Free-coefficient classification by multiplicities is the corrected statement.','false as stated','proof_audit.md §1 verifies invertibility, connectedness and nonprincipality by the norm obstruction a²+5b²=2.','C','Search S137-09/10 and Grothendieck bibliography: classical module/projective distinctions and SGA6 I4.8 preserve actual projective modules. No numerical-rank theorem with the literal generality is possible.','Projective-module framework established before1975/76; counterexample checked2026.','Refuted general rank classification; CL-SA09-137-009(corrected) retains module isomorphism classes or restricts to free coefficients.',['SGA6I','StacksPerfect'])
add(10,[],[12,13,15],T1+':424-460;518-544','f(−1)=χ; coefficients entiers','The Newton polynomials binom(t,j), not ordinary integral-coefficient monomials, form a Z-basis of integer-valued polynomials. With prescribed finite ν_j, realizability by nonnegative disk multiplicities requires the expansion of f−Σν_jbinom(t,j) in binom(t+1,i) to have μ₀=0 and μ_i≥0. Then f(−1)=Σ(−1)^jν_j.','proof sketched','outputs/recompute.json DK_rank, Euler_at_minus_one; proof_audit.md §§1,6. binom(t,2)=(t²−t)/2 diagnoses the inserted coefficient phrase.','E','Search S137-09/12: the elementary Newton argument is independently checked; PursuingStacks§119 later explicitly uses the integer-valued binomial basis, and Toën2020§2 uses the same algebra. Neither source equates Int(Z) with Z[t].','Newton basis classical before manuscript; Grothendieck1983§119; Toën2019 preprint/2020 publication.','Valid over the integer-valued polynomial lattice; the ordinary Z[t] reading is false.',['GrothendieckPS1983','Toen2020'])
add(11,[],[14,15],T1+':474-510;518-544','(str.) ∂-pseudo-cohérent; (str.) ∂-parfait','Strict ∂-pseudocoherence means finite-projective normalized terms; strict ∂-perfection additionally means bounded normalization. Finite-projective simplicial terms are equivalent to finite-projective normalized terms. The filtration by normalized degree reconstructs the complex from spheres. Derived variants mean existence of such models up to quasi-isomorphism.','proof sketched','proof_audit.md §2 checks the finite direct-sum/direct-summand implications and distinguishes strict from derived.','E','Search S137-02/09/10: SGA6 I2.1 and I4.7-4.8 predate these notes and distinguish strict representatives from derived perfection; Stacks064N/0656 preserve that distinction.','SGA6 seminar1966/67; publication1971.','Valid after keeping the source’s strict and derived senses apart.',['SGA6I','StacksPseudo','StacksPerfect','StacksDK'])
add(12,[],[14],T1+':503-510','pseudo-cohérent ssi les L_n sont de type fini','The ordinary derived-pseudocoherent condition cannot be equivalent to finite generation of every term of an arbitrary representative. An identity disk on an infinite-rank free module is contractible and hence perfect, but its simplicial terms are not finitely generated. Over a noetherian ring, degreewise finite terms of a nonnegative complex imply pseudocoherence in the corresponding bounded-above cochain convention; the converse fails for representatives.','false as stated','proof_audit.md §2 gives the explicit infinite-free disk and verifies quasi-isomorphism to0.','C','Search S137-02/09/10: SGA6 I2.1-2.2 and Stacks064N define pseudocoherence through a finite-free resolution, not arbitrary representative terms.','SGA6 1966/67, published1971; counterexample audit2026.','Refuted literal iff; CL-SA09-137-012(corrected) is the resolution-based condition.',['SGA6I','StacksPseudo'])
add(13,[],[14,15],T1+':503-510;518-544','k noethérien régulier ... ρ(n) polynôme','Pointwise polynomial rank growth of residue-field fibers does not characterize derived ∂-perfection without uniformity and representative controls. Over Z, N_i=Z/p_i in each i≥1, zero differential, gives finite simplicial terms and a polynomial at each fiber but unbounded homology. Conversely ⊕_{r≥0}D_{2r+1}(Z) is contractible and has rank2^n.','false as stated','outputs/recompute.json nonuniform_fiber_ranks and infinite_contractible_rank; proof_audit.md §2 proves the infinite examples and checks noetherian regular base Z.','C','Search S137-02/09/10: SGA6 I4.7-4.8 and Stacks0656 require bounded finite-projective models. SGA6’s perfect-amplitude formulation supplies the missing uniform bound; ordinary fiber rank of a chosen representative is not derived invariant.','SGA6 1966/67,1971; explicit counterexamples2026.','Both directions fail literally; corrected derived criterion is CL-SA09-137-013(corrected): pseudocoherence plus finite Tor-amplitude, not pointwise rank growth alone.',['SGA6I','StacksPerfect'])
add(14,[],[15,17],T1+':518-544;637-638','on peut ... épimorphisme; (str.) parfait','A perfect complex admits a bounded finite-projective model, but a bounded model need not surject degreewise onto an arbitrary unbounded contractible representative. The same infinite identity-disk sum has a nonzero normalized term in every degree, precluding such a surjection. Finite-brick support characterizes strict perfection of that representative, not derived perfection.','false as stated','proof_audit.md §2; outputs/recompute.json infinite_contractible_rank. Exactness of normalization transfers a hypothetical epimorphism to impossible degreewise surjections.','C','Search S137-02/09/10: SGA6 I4.1-4.8 concerns maps up to homotopy and quasi-isomorphic bounded models; it does not imply epimorphic bounded replacements of every representative.','SGA6 1966/67,1971; refined reading2026.','Existence of a bounded model is valid; epimorphic and representative-finiteness additions are refuted. Refinement: CL-SA09-137-014(corrected).',['SGA6I','StacksPerfect'])
add(15,[],[16,17,18,19,20],T1+':573-775','k principal; facteurs élémentaires; Φ(i,n)','Over a PID, every nonnegative complex of finite-free modules is a degreewise locally finite direct sum of identity disks, nonunit scalar disks D_i(a), and free spheres. The invariant factors of B_i⊂Z_i, with units separated, determine its isomorphism class. A bounded complex has finitely many factors. Flasque/acyclic complexes contain only identity disks; categorical projectives may also have S₀.','proved there','proof_audit.md §3 explains successive Smith normal forms and the acyclic/projective cases.','E','Search S137-09: Rasmussen–Marchand2019 §3.3, Theorem3.23 and Corollary3.25, explicitly prove the same decomposition; the source itself gives the classical PID proof. This is ordinary chain isomorphism, not only a derived classification.','Elementary divisor theory predates manuscript; opened explicit treatment2019.','Valid with PID and finite-free hypotheses; not a rank-only theorem over general rings.',['RasmussenMarchand2019','DoldPuppe1961'])
add(16,[],[17],T1+':631-635','μ_{i+1}+β_{i+1}+ν_i+β_i','The displayed normalized-rank expression omits μ_i. The corrected formula is rank N_i=μ_{i+1}+β_{i+1}+ν_i+μ_i+β_i. One identity disk D₁(Z) has rank1 in degree1 while the transcribed expression gives0.','false as stated','outputs/recompute.json missing_mu_i_rank_formula; proof_audit.md §3.','C','Search S137-09: the two-term decomposition of Rasmussen–Marchand§3.3 confirms both adjacent disk contributions. This is an arithmetic/index defect, not an open classification question.','Classical decomposition; correction audited2026.','False displayed formula; corrected expression identified as CL-SA09-137-016(corrected), with scan decision deferred.',['RasmussenMarchand2019'])
add(17,[],[19],T1+':703-742','H_{i−1}=k/(n); ρ=binom(t+1,i)','The scalar disk D_i(n) has H_{i−1}=k/(n) and other homology zero for nonzero n in a PID. Its simplicial rank equals binom(t+1,i) independently of n. Thus Hilbert ranks plus free-homology ranks and merely the number of torsion invariant factors cannot determine the complex: D₁(2) and D₁(3) differ. Actual invariant factors are required.','false as stated','outputs/recompute.json torsion_counts_not_invariants; proof_audit.md §3 separates the true disk calculation from the false numerical completeness claim.','C','Search S137-09: Smith-normal-form classification in Rasmussen–Marchand§3.3 retains the invariant-factor values. The source’s disk homology computation is valid; only the final coarse-invariant assertion is refuted.','Classical PID theorem; counterexample verified2026.','Refinement CL-SA09-137-017(corrected): use invariant-factor values up to associates, not their count.',['RasmussenMarchand2019','StacksDK'])
add(18,[],[20,21,22,23,24,25,26,27],T1+':746-1188','Hom(Φ(i,n),L); qm−pn; compositions','For finite-free nonnegative complexes over a PID, Hom(D_i(n),L) consists of pairs (x,y) with d x=n y and d y=0; identifying with x alone requires n a nonzerodivisor and torsion-free target terms. For scalar disks, Hom(D_i(n),D_j(m)) is rank1 when j=i or i+1 and zero otherwise; at equal degree m q=n p. Sphere-to-disk maps occur at j=i+1, disk-to-sphere at target degree i, and sphere-to-sphere only at equal degree. Composition is componentwise multiplication and matrices.','proof sketched','outputs/recompute.json disk_Hom_same_degree/disk_Hom_degree_table; proof_audit.md §3 proves all degree cases and the scalar obstruction.','E','Search S137-09/11: standard chain-map equations in the opened PID treatment and Dold–Puppe equivalence suffice. No separate later theorem is needed; ratios and extension-class labels in the source must be type-checked against m q=n p.','Classical chain algebra before manuscript; explicit recomputation2026.','Valid under the precise nonzerodivisor/PID conditions; doubtful arrow and ratio labels remain Stage4 alarms.',['RasmussenMarchand2019','DoldPuppe1961'])
add(19,[],[23,24,25,26,27,28],T1+':896-1209','axiomes; e_i; compositions évidentes','Elementary objects, their Hom modules, extension generators and matrix compositions reconstruct the finite additive category once the stated brick decomposition holds. Ext¹ and the meaning of extension generators require an ambient abelian/exact category; the listed finite-generation axiom cannot simultaneously cover all modules. Tensor and Γ reconstruction are left as additional work.','open on the pages','proof_audit.md §3 checks the matrix-composition core; no verification of an unspecified exact structure is claimed.','C','Search S137-03/09/11: Isbell1960 treats adequate subcategories; Bühler2008/2009 gives exact-category requirements. Neither identifies this exact package of generators, Ext symbols and finiteness axioms without reconstruction.','Isbell1960; Bühler first circulation2008, opened version2009.','Additive core standard; intrinsic Ext axiomatization and nonlinear structures remain incompletely specified.',['Isbell1960','Buhler2009'],'medium')
add(20,[],[29],T1+':1213-1236','tout objet ... limite inductive ... équivalent','Mere existence of some colimit presentation from a full subcategory A does not imply density or full faithfulness of C→Set^{Aop}. For finite-dimensional Q-vector spaces and A={Q}, every object is a finite coproduct of A, but a scalar-homogeneous nonadditive map Q²→Q gives a natural transformation of restricted nerves not induced by a linear map. Canonical A/X-colimit density or additive enrichment repairs it.','false as stated','outputs/recompute.json false_density; proof_audit.md §4 checks naturality for every scalar including0 and explicit failure of additivity.','C','Search S137-03/04: Isbell1960, introductory adequacy definition and §1, distinguishes full faithfulness of the restricted nerve from mere generation. Its precise stronger condition matches the corrected claim.','Isbell received1959, revised/published1960.','Refuted implication; CL-SA09-137-020(corrected) requires density, or uses the enriched additive finite envelope.',['Isbell1960'])
add(21,[],[30,31,32,33,34],T1+':1253-1398','enveloppe additive; sommes finies','The finite additive envelope of a k-linear category is modeled by finite direct sums of representable modules; matrices of original morphisms provide composition. For one object this is the category of finite-free right modules over its endomorphism ring, with variance fixed. Restriction of additive functors to generators is fully faithful and essentially surjective onto compatible k-linear data when the target has finite sums.','proof sketched','proof_audit.md §4 gives the matrix extension.','E','Search S137-03/04/13: Isbell1960’s adequate-subcategory formalism and the matrix construction identify the finite additive case. The much broader all-functor restriction assertion on scan34 does not follow without colimit-preservation assumptions.','Isbell1960; finite-additive construction classical before1975/76.','Valid finite additive-envelope theorem; no arbitrary colimit-completion theorem is inferred.',['Isbell1960'])
add(22,[],[31,32,33,34,35,36],T1+':1278-1458','dualité; co-présheaves; Hom; ⊗','The proposed presheaf/co-presheaf duality can be made precise on objects whose canonical Isbell units are isomorphisms. Arbitrary presheaves are not all reflexive. Finite weighted tensor and Hom pairings are represented in an additive target when the indicated finite sums and kernels exist; this is ordinary Hom, not derived Hom.','stated without proof','proof_audit.md §4 treats finite representables and variance; no arbitrary coend-existence theorem is proved.','C','Search S137-03/04: Isbell1960 §§1.3-1.5 provides the conjugacy/reflexivity formalism. The source’s unrestricted generation language requires the density repair of CL-SA09-137-020.','Isbell1960, preceding manuscript.','Correct finite/reflexive core; broad equivalences need additional density and representability hypotheses.',['Isbell1960'],'medium')
add(23,[],[36,37,38],T1+':1462-1547','F_X(M)=Hom(X,M); reconstruct ... Γ','Knowing F on the elementary disks determines its values on the finite additive envelope. Recovering values on spheres or torsion disks via presentations further requires preservation of the relevant kernels. The proposed extraction of tensor and Γ operations from an ordinary cochain complex asks for additional compatible structure; an arbitrary additive functor does not supply it.','open on the pages','proof_audit.md §§4-6 separates the additive generator argument from preserved-kernel and nonlinear obligations.','C','Search S137-03/04/06/13: Isbell’s restricted nerve and Dold–Puppe do not supply nonlinear enrichment automatically. Horel/Mandell reconstruction applies only after specific structured cochains are given.','Isbell1960; Dold–Puppe1961; modern comparisons2003/2006,2022/2024.','Additive reconstruction established with exactness; the structured reconstruction is the manuscript programme, not a theorem of plain complexes.',['Isbell1960','DoldPuppe1961','Mandell2006','Horel2024'],'medium')
add(24,[50,53,54,56,65],[39,73,74],T1+':1551-1567; '+T2+':998-1002','dans quelle mesure; il est clair','The author asks whether enriched cochains are determined by de Rham–Sullivan or PD de Rham data and how much of the homotopy type they recover, while asserting the reverse determination informally. No enhancement-preserving comparison functor, localization, class of spaces or integral equivalence is specified.','open on the pages','No manuscript computation to redo; proof_audit.md §6 tests only truncation, denominators and product levels.','C','Search S137-06/12: Sullivan1977 Theorem10.1 handles rational nilpotent finite-type data. Mandell2006 MainTheorem and0.1 recognize finite-type nilpotent spaces via integral E∞ cochains; Horel2024 Theorem5.4 uses cosimplicial binomial rings; Toën2020 Theorem0.1 assumes simply connected finite type. None identifies the exact strict manuscript input.','Sullivan manuscript before1977 publication; Mandell first circulation2003/publication2006; Toën2019/2020; Horel2022/2024.','Modern reconstruction is substantial but does not settle the missing archival comparison. Ordinary chain complexes or binary homotopies alone are insufficient.',['Sullivan1977','Mandell2006','Horel2024','Toen2020'],'high')
add(25,[1],[40,41,44,45],T1+':1571-1587;1690-1785;1955-1997; '+T2+':10-47','Prop. 1; va à l’identité, qfd.','The finite additive envelope of the walking nonnegative cochain complex is universal for cochain objects in any additive k-linear target. Its disk realization has End(C^n)=k, Hom(C^n,C^{n+1})=k d_n, other Hom groups zero, and d_{n+1}d_n=0. Evaluation/reconstruction is checked on generators, then finite sums.','proved there','proof_audit.md §4; disk Hom degree tables in outputs/recompute.json.','E','Search S137-03/13: the matrix universal property is classical; Hua2026 pp164-165 also gives this exact disk Hom calculation within the evaluation theorem. No Lean source was run here.','Underlying construction classical; exact public archival treatmentNovember2026.','Valid ordinary additive statement; infinite sums and arbitrary idempotent completion are not implicit.',['Isbell1960','Hua2026'])
add(26,[],[41,42],T1+':1727-1763;1789-1827','C ... karoubienne [cancelled]; facteurs directs libres','The cancelled unconditional claim that the finite-free disk category is Karoubian fails over k=k₁×k₂: the idempotent(1,0) on a free disk has projective nonfree image. The later hypothesis that direct summands of finite-free modules are free repairs this particular issue; passing to all finite projectives gives the Karoubi envelope.','corrected by himself later','proof_audit.md §4 gives the explicit product-ring idempotent and module-rank distinction.','E','Search S137-02/03/13: SGA6 I4.8 uses finite projectives, and Bühler§6 treats idempotent completion. The source itself recognizes the extra freeness condition on42.','SGA6 published1971; Bühler2008/2009 later systematic treatment.','The deleted unrestricted claim is false; surviving restricted statement and projective completion are valid.',['SGA6I','Buhler2009'])
add(27,[],[42,43],T1+':1789-1869;1924-1951','Prop. 2 ... dualité parfaite ... par composition','The transcribed same-index pairing Hom(C^n,M)×Hom(M,C^n)→k is not perfect: M=C^{n+1} gives k×0. A shifted second target C^{n+1} yields the expected pairing into k d_n on finite disk sums. The α/β variances and boundary sphere at degree0 must be fixed before stating the claimed duality.','false as stated','outputs/recompute.json same_index_pairing; proof_audit.md §4.','C','Search S137-03/13: disk Hom computations also appear in Hua2026 p164; the source’s Proposition2 is explicitly outside that paper’s claimed verification. No published same-index theorem can match the literal formula.','Underlying finite duality classical; explicit archival check2026.','Refuted literal same-index pairing; CL-SA09-137-027(corrected) is the stated shifted candidate, pending ink review.',['Hua2026','DoldPuppe1961'])
add(28,[1,8],[44,45,56,57],T1+':1955-1997; '+T2+':1-47;530-543','Hom^•_k(K^•,C^•); vérification ... élémentaire','For a bounded finite-free complex K, the object of degree-zero cochain maps into a B-valued complex is represented by the kernel of ∏Hom(K^i,C^i)→∏Hom(K^i,C^{i+1}), δu=du−ud, when these finite products/cotensors and kernels exist. For a universal finite sum of disks, representation follows without arbitrary kernels. Transpose Hom(λ,L)≅Hom(L∨,λ∨) requires only L bounded finite free, not λ reflexive.','proof sketched','proof_audit.md §§4-5 checks the representing equations and degreewise transpose. The line continues across the package boundary; it is not an unfinished formula.','E','Search S137-03/13: finite duality and the universal property yield the formula; Hua2026 p165 uses the same L∨ cochain-map representation but does not claim formal verification of source Proposition3.','Classical finite duality; contemporary comparison2026.','Valid with the displayed representability conditions; superscript dot denotes ordinary cochain-map object rather than a derived mapping complex.',['Hua2026','Isbell1960'])
add(29,[2],[46,47],T2+':51-141','Dold-Puppe; Si B est karoubienne','Propositions4-5 transport the universal cochain construction to simplicial/cosimplicial objects. For an idempotent-complete additive k-linear target, the required normalization idempotents split and the equivalence is available; otherwise only the stated fully faithful functor with restricted essential image is justified. The manuscript’s old half-simplicial terminology is interpreted using its Dold–Puppe reference, not replaced by faces-only semisimplicial objects.','proof sketched','proof_audit.md §1 and §4; Stacks019D normalization construction was read.','E','Search S137-01/13: Dold–Puppe1961 §3 (especially the normalization/inverse construction) predates the notes; Stacks019D proves the abelian case. The additive Karoubian extension follows by the same split-idempotent formulas, not arbitrary kernels.','1958 announcement;1961 full publication.','Valid with split idempotents and the intended simplicial convention; the weaker target claim must retain its image restriction.',['DoldPuppe1961','StacksDK'])
add(30,[3,75],[49,50,60,61],T2+':154-254;686-708','Sex1; Sex2; Il faut peut-être exiger qu’un composé','The initial class Σ is stable under isomorphism/finite sums and contains split kernel–cokernel sequences; closure under composition of admissible maps is queried. Pushout/pullback stability is introduced later. These first two axioms alone do not constitute the complete modern exact-category axioms, and the marginal claim that one condition suffices has uncertain scope.','open on the pages','Axiom-by-axiom comparison with Bühler Definition2.1 was performed; no theorem about an undeciphered minimal axiom system was inferred.','C','Search S137-05/11: Bühler2008/2009 Definition2.1 lists identities, composition and pushout/pullback closure. It supports the corrected exact-category framework but does not validate the unreadable redundancy claim.','Quillen framework1973; opened exposition first circulation2008, version2009.','The missing axioms must be supplied explicitly before relative homological theorems are invoked.',['Buhler2009'],'high')

add(31,[4,5,6,68,70],[51,52,53,54,55,56],T2+':258-528','est pleinement fidèle; σρ≃id','Let P=Ch≥0^b(finite-free k-modules), Σ=degreewise exact sequences, and C^n=D_{n+1}(k). For additive k-linear B, evaluation F↦F(C•) on Σ-left-exact functors is fully faithful. If B has kernels, every cochain object is represented by σ(E)(L)=Hom_cochains(L∨,E), so evaluation is an equivalence. In the original relative formulation, the image is restricted by the requisite admissible kernels.','proof sketched','proof_audit.md §5 gives the finite disk/kernel proof and checks the counit on generators. It does not fill arbitrary-relative-Σ gaps.','B','Search S137-13: Hua2026 pp164-165 treats this precise P, proves full faithfulness and the kernel-bearing additive-target equivalence, while excluding the general relative variant. This contemporary preprint is a reported treatment, not independent evidence of established priority; its reported Lean verification was not rerun. Our ordinary targeted proof check confirms the stated restricted theorem.','Public preprintNovember2026; no earlier exact publication located in S137-03/13 searches.','Restricted additive theorem supported by the ordinary proof check and the opened contemporary preprint; broad relative essential-image formulation still needs its explicit admissibility hypotheses.',['Hua2026','Buhler2009'],'high')
add(32,[7],[51,56],T2+':278-301;523-528','F est Σ-exact ssi C• est une Σ₀-résolution; du moins si B cat. abélienne','When B is abelian and Σ₀ is all short exact sequences, the evaluated cochain complex is acyclic in positive degrees exactly when the associated functor sends the admissible source short exact sequences to short exact sequences. The author expressly limits the verified form to this case; general relative targets require more.','proof sketched','Use 0→S_{n−1}→D_n→S_n→0: the image condition is im d^{n−1}=ker d^n. Conversely finite filtrations reduce a source exact sequence to these disk/sphere checks; proof_audit.md §5 gives the representability framework.','C','Search S137-05/13: Bühler§12 supports relative resolution methods once exact axioms hold; Hua2026 p165 explicitly excludes this part(b) from its claimed formal verification. The abelian case has the elementary criterion above; no exact unrestricted match located.','Classical abelian resolution theory predates1975/76; exact archival treatment remains limited2026.','Valid abelian-target form; general relative form open on these pages and not settled by the searched exact match.',['Buhler2009','Hua2026'],'medium')
add(33,[9,10,11],[58,59,60,61,63],T2+':547-684;709-725;764','Construction intrinsèque de P; L_i,Z_i,B_i,H_i','The intrinsic characterization is revised and partly cancelled. The category generated by finite sums of disks and spheres has free/projective homology; the category of all bounded finite-free complexes also contains [Z --2--> Z]. Omitting H on60 and including H for P on61 cannot both describe the same original P. Condition b and the exactness test remain too uncertain to yield one complete axiom system.','false as stated','proof_audit.md §5 gives the bounded finite-free counterexample and the exact P/Q distinction. The cancelled59 proof is documentary, not a surviving theorem.','F','Search S137-05/11/13: Bühler’s exact axioms and Hua2026’s explicitly defined P do not resolve the conflicting manuscript categories or uncertain b). A restricted object characterization is elementary, but the full intended axiom system is not identifiable.','Compared with2008/2009 exact-category exposition and2026 exact P treatment.','Literal P-image statement fails; the author’s exact intended replacement remains unidentified. Refined object claim: CL-SA09-137-033(corrected).',['Buhler2009','Hua2026'],'medium')
add(34,[12],[37,62],T1+':1495; '+T2+':729-760','C abélienne; un bimorphisme n’est pas néc. un iso','Bounded finite-free complexes over a PID have kernels represented by finite-free complexes; the inclusion of the kernel in the source is degreewise split because the image is free. The category is not abelian: multiplication2 on Z[0] is a noninvertible bimorphism. The general-ring kernel assertion is not justified without projectivity/coherence conditions.','corrected by himself later','proof_audit.md §5 checks kernel splitting under PID and the bimorphism, including all finite-free test objects.','E','Search S137-09/11: elementary PID submodule theory in Rasmussen–Marchand§3.3 gives the kernel claim. Bühler’s exact-category framework does not require an abelian category.','Classical PID facts predate manuscript; Bühler2008/2009 organizes the distinction.','The nonabelian warning is correct; any erased or contextual abelian expansion must remain withdrawn.',['RasmussenMarchand2019','Buhler2009'])
add(35,[13,14],[63,64],T2+':764-770','P₀ les injectifs; projectifs ... rajouter Ψ⁰; une seule classe d’homotopie','Against degreewise split exact sequences of finite-free complexes, positive disks are relatively injective and projective; the degree-zero sphere is additionally projective in the nonnegative category. Enough resolutions and uniqueness up to homotopy of augmented comparisons are asserted. The proposed Q restriction and Ext=hyperext require an exact structure supporting those resolutions.','stated without proof','proof_audit.md §5 checks the disk Hom arguments and shows Q is not extension-closed in P via 0→Z[0]→[Z --2--> Z]→Z[1]→0. General Ext comparison was not certified.','C','Search S137-05/11: Bühler Theorem12.4 proves resolution comparison in an exact category with enough projectives (dually injectives). Its hypotheses are stronger than the page’s initial Σ axioms; they must be checked for the actual Q.','Classical resolution theorem; exact-category formulation1973 onward, opened2009 version.','Generator calculations and conditional comparison theorem valid; the exact Q/Ext identification remains a stated gap.',['Buhler2009'],'medium')
add(36,[15],[64,65],T2+':772-778','on doit pouvoir montrer; sauf erreur','For the indicated left-exact functor category, the author proposes that right-derived evaluation at Ψ⁰ is computed by the cochain complex F(C•), and suggests passage to derived categories. A sufficient modern formulation needs an abelian functor category, enough injectives or an adapted acyclic resolution class, and exact evaluation where used.','open on the pages','No numerical computation; proof_audit.md §5 identifies the missing derived-functor ambient hypotheses.','C','Search S137-05/11/13: Bühler§12 supplies resolution machinery; Hua2026 treats ordinary evaluation only. Neither opened source proves the exact derived-category assertion for the manuscript’s relative target. No claim of a known unrestricted equivalence is made.','Classical derived-functor framework precedes manuscript; exact formulation not located as of2026.','Plausible under a specified abelian/acyclic setup; the bare additive formulation is insufficient.',['Buhler2009','Hua2026'],'medium')
add(37,[17,18],[65,66],T2+':782-809','produit tensoriel ... notation *; Ψ⁰','Transport degreewise tensor of simplicial modules through normalization to a symmetric monoidal product *. It is distinct from ordinary total tensor but homotopy equivalent by Eilenberg–Zilber. Its unit is S₀. Contractible objects form a tensor ideal with projective factors, and S_i*S_j has the same homology as S_{i+j}, with contractible summands under the splitting hypotheses.','proof sketched','proof_audit.md §§1,6; outputs/recompute.json AW_interval tests why ordinary total-cochain products are not strictly identified.','E','Search S137-01/11: Dold–Puppe1961 §2 provides the precise generalized Eilenberg–Zilber comparison. The source’s co-idéal wording and other-input clause are reading alarms, not a new algebraic theorem.','Eilenberg–Zilber1953; Dold–Puppe1961.','Valid transported monoidal structure and comparison; direct-sum/free refinements retain the appropriate splitting assumptions.',['DoldPuppe1961'])
add(38,[19,20],[66,67],T2+':811-848','structure multiplicative sur F; 1_B→F(1_B′)','The displayed natural multiplication F(X)⊗F(Y)→F(X⊗Y), unit1→F(1), and associativity/symmetry/unit diagrams define a symmetric lax monoidal functor. They induce commutative algebra objects from commutative algebra objects, compose, and admit multiplicative natural transformations. The unit map is not required invertible.','proved there','The algebra-object product and unit axioms follow by substituting multiplication/unit into the diagrams. proof_audit.md §6 distinguishes lax from strong.','E','Search S137-05/06/13 and SGA4 XVII5.5: this is the usual monoidal-functor construction; the defining diagrams themselves give a direct proof. No new strictification or derived full-faithfulness result is asserted.','Monoidal-category formalism predates1975/76; exact terminology is modern.','Valid formal consequence of the explicit diagrams; a strong-unit contextual expansion overstates the page.',['SGA4XVII','DoldPuppe1961'])
add(39,[21,22],[67,68,69,70,71],T2+':850-972','str. mul. demi-simpliciale; K n’a pas d’unité pour *!','Multiplicative data on pairs of universal generators can be expressed as bicomplex/simplicial-compatible maps. The initial nonunital K cannot support the unital definition; the author adjoins S₀ through P₀ or Q and asks for a closed degree-zero unit, with a final kernel-free variant indicated.','corrected by himself later','Generator determination follows the matrix proof in proof_audit.md §4; the missing unit is S₀, not a finite sum of positive acyclic disks.','C','Search S137-01/06/13: Dold–Puppe describes the simplicial comparison; Berger–Fresse gives a later coherent cochain enhancement, not this exact strict generator equivalence. No opened source removes the source’s unit enlargement.','Dold–Puppe1961; Berger–Fresse first circulation2001, publication2004.','Generator formulas and identified unit obstruction are sound; equivalence with a full category of structured cochains requires the omitted coherence and extension steps.',['DoldPuppe1961','BergerFresse2004'],'medium')
add(40,[23,24,82],[70,71],T2+':941-972','d’où la détermination unique de ?; indépendant ... immédiat','The proposed product extension from injective generators is uniquely determined if it factors through the right-hand monomorphism. Monicity alone does not prove existence. A sufficient repair assumes X*Y is the admissible kernel of I₀*J₀→(I₁*J₀)⊕(I₀*J₁) and F preserves it; naturality then gives the factorization. Independence, associativity and symmetry depend on that existence.','stated without proof','proof_audit.md §6 proves the conditional kernel repair, explicitly not the missing general tensor-kernel property.','C','Search S137-05/06/11/13: exact-category and operadic-cochain references furnish surrounding techniques; no exact unrestricted factorization theorem for the page’s P/Q and target was identified. Modern E∞ operations do not supply this strict factorization automatically.','Relevant exact/operadic developments2001-2009; exact archival gap remains2026.','Uniqueness is proved; existence is a real local proof obligation. Conditional corrected statement CL-SA09-137-040(corrected) is checked.',['Buhler2009','BergerFresse2004'],'high')
add(41,[25,26],[72],T2+':977-994','le tout à homotopie près; signes','Resolution comparison yields a multiplication on C•⊗C•→C•, with associativity, signed commutativity and unity up to homotopy, hence a graded-commutative product on cohomology where defined. The stated separate homotopies do not specify a coherent E∞ algebra, and they do not give a strictly commutative integral cochain product.','proof sketched','outputs/recompute.json AW_interval; proof_audit.md §6. The edge computation refutes an overstrong reading, not the author’s homotopy-qualified claim.','B','Search S137-06: Berger–Fresse, Introduction and cochain-action construction, supplies an explicit Barratt–Eccles E∞ action on normalized cochains. This develops higher coherent operations; it is stronger data in a specific cochain model, not proof of the manuscript’s strict extension.','arXiv first version2001; openedv2 October2002; publication2004.','Standard cohomological product; coherent enhancement established for standard cochains, with exact archival comparison still separate.',['BergerFresse2004','DoldPuppe1961'])
add(42,[30,97],[74],T2+':1002','Il y a donc un complexe de De Rham-Sullivan en Car.0','A characteristic-zero de Rham–Sullivan conclusion is announced without expanding the coefficient hypotheses. A usual identification of divided and symmetric powers by γ_n(x)=x^n/n! requires a Q-algebra, not characteristic0 alone. The page does not explicitly assert that formula over every characteristic-zero ring.','stated without proof','proof_audit.md §6: Z has characteristic0 but 1/2 does not exist. This is a hypothesis alarm, not a refutation of an unstated fully quantified theorem.','C','Search S137-06/12: Sullivan1977 §10 works with Q-polynomial forms and nilpotent finite-type spaces. Grothendieck1966 Theorem1 works over C; neither supports replacing Q-algebras by arbitrary characteristic-zero rings.','Grothendieck letter1963/publication1966; Sullivan1977.','Rational version has established models; literal short sentence is under-specified.',['Sullivan1977','Grothendieck1966'],'medium')
add(43,[31,43],[75,83,86],T2+':1023-1030;1254-1265;1304-1310','(f+g)∘h=f∘h+g∘h','With finite products and an additive degree-one category, addition on nonlinear Hom sets is induced by the linear fold map and is additive in the outer variable of composition. Dependence on the inner variable is generally polynomial, not additive. Thus the full polynomial category is not automatically preadditive.','proved there','proof_audit.md §6 derives the fold-map addition and homogeneous substitution formula.','E','Search S137-07/13: Roby’s laws (SGA4 XVII5.5.2.2-3) give the module model; Hua2026 p167 checks the homogeneous additive/product core but not mixed-degree total composition.','Roby1963; SGA4 1973; contemporary homogeneous audit2026.','Valid one-sided additivity; an inserted bilinear reading would contradict the nonlinear model.',['Roby1963','SGA4XVII','Hua2026'])
add(44,[32,33,34,87],[75,76,77,86],T2+':1036-1119;1304-1310','n’est ... pas unique; Oubli','The attempted recovery of a grading from integer-scalar weights is false in torsion and is withdrawn: over F_p, λ^p=λ. The decomposition is extra data; testing polynomial laws over every coefficient algebra distinguishes T from T^p. The degree-one/multidegree compatibility is separately flagged as omitted.','corrected by himself later','outputs/recompute.json Fp_scalar_weights; proof_audit.md §6 checks both scalar equality and polynomial-law distinction.','E','Search S137-07/08: Roby1963 and SGA4 XVII5.5.2.2 define laws over all base algebras. Friedlander–Suslin1997 §2 distinguishes strict polynomial structure from values of functions; it does not justify the cancelled scalar uniqueness.','Roby1963 before manuscript; Friedlander–Suslin1997 later structured-functor theory.','Retraction correct; all-base-algebras condition is mathematically decisive and the source’s extra grading must be retained.',['Roby1963','SGA4XVII','FriedlanderSuslin1997'])
add(45,[35,36,37,38,89,90],[77,78,79,80],T2+':1096-1198','foncteur triadditif; renforcer la propriété universelle; Γ⁰(0)','The tensor object represents multidegree(1,1) maps and Γ^p represents homogeneous maps in the degree-one category. Strict representability requires these properties to persist with all additional parameters. Under coherent multidegree/exponential comparison isomorphisms and idempotent splitting, homogeneous summands are representable and Γ⁰(0) serves as tensor unit. Triadditivity and reduction from binary to all arities need the corresponding compatibility axioms.','proof sketched','proof_audit.md §6 gives the Yoneda/idempotent and fold/unit arguments, conditional on the stated coherence.','C','Search S137-07/08/13: Roby/SGA4 XVII5.5.2.3 and5.5.2.6 prove the module representability/exponential model. They do not establish the full arbitrary-category minimal axiom theorem. Hua2026 expressly leaves the full tensor/multidegree equivalence unverified.','Roby1963; SGA4 1973; exact broad axiom audit still incomplete2026.','Module example established; abstract theorem remains conditional on coherence and strict parameter stability.',['Roby1963','SGA4XVII','Hua2026'],'medium')
add(46,[39],[80,81],T2+':1190;1203-1208','transformant sommes en ⊗; algèbre graduée commutative','A coherent exponential functor Γ* from direct sums to tensor products turns the fold map X⊕X→X and zero object into a graded-commutative algebra structure on Γ*(X). Coassociative comultiplication and antipode are a further conditional Hopf extension made by the earlier note, not the manuscript assertion.','proof sketched','proof_audit.md §6 gives the fold/zero argument; outputs/recompute.json IntZ_leading_product is a separate earlier-run comparison.','E','Search S137-07/08: SGA4 XVII5.5.2.6 records the exponential formula for modules, and Roby’s divided-power algebra supplies the classical example. No Hopf theorem is attributed to the manuscript.','Roby1963; SGA4 1973.','Valid commutative graded-algebra consequence of coherent exponential data.',['Roby1963','SGA4XVII'])
add(47,[40,41],[81,82,83],T2+':1211-1265','g∘f=g Γ^q(f) α_(q,p)','Natural maps α_{p,q}:Γ^{pq}→Γ^pΓ^q with the typed coassociativity square and Γ¹-unit identities define associative composition on homogeneous arrows P_p(X,Y)=Hom(Γ^pX,Y). Conversely homogeneous representability yields these α maps by factoring universal arrows; the two constructions are inverse up to canonical isomorphism.','proof sketched','proof_audit.md §6 checks substitution/naturality associativity. Stage4 records the ill-typed superscript on one edge of the source square.','B','Search S137-07/13: Hua2026 pp166-167 explicitly treats precisely this homogeneous core and distinguishes it from the full tensor-polynomial equivalence. This contemporary preprint is a reported treatment; we checked the ordinary categorical argument, not the reported Lean build or any priority claim.','Exact public archival treatmentNovember2026; no earlier exact source located by title/back-reference searches.','Homogeneous core established with correctly typed α and unit axioms; no conclusion about mixed-degree sums follows.',['Hua2026','Roby1963'])
add(48,[42,91],[82,83],T2+':1240-1274','α_(q,0) ... isom.; Je l’avais oublié','The constant-degree condition α_{q,0}:1→Γ^q(1) being invertible is added independently of Γ¹≅id. It is required for the intended constant maps and cannot be suppressed by proving only positive-degree homogeneous associativity.','corrected by himself later','proof_audit.md §6; outputs/recompute.json constant_substitution shows why top positive-degree data lose constant behavior.','C','Search S137-07/08/13: Roby’s laws include degree0; SGA4 XVII5.5.2 gives this module model. Hua2026’s homogeneous core does not construct the total mixed-degree category. The source itself acknowledges the omission.','Roby1963; explicit source correction on83; partial exact treatment2026.','The omitted condition is a genuine independent requirement in the author’s converse construction.',['Roby1963','SGA4XVII','Hua2026'])
add(49,[44,92],[84],T2+':1278-1284','Les deux notions sont donc en équivalence','The full equivalence claimed between strict polynomial categories and additive tensor-PD categories requires compatible products, Hom addition, all multidegrees, strict parameter-stable tensor/Γ representations, constants, and mixed-degree composition. The homogeneous co-Kleisli construction proves only part of this assertion.','stated without proof','proof_audit.md §6 checks the homogeneous restriction only; no construction of the mixed-degree total category was made in this consolidation.','C','Search S137-07/08/13: Roby and Friedlander–Suslin establish concrete polynomial-law/strict-functor theories, not this arbitrary-category equivalence. Hua2026 pp166-168 identifies the same limitation. No opened reference completes the exact full list of manuscript structures.','Roby1963; Friedlander–Suslin1997; exact homogeneous partial development2026.','A precisely delimited unresolved axiom/comparison task, not a claim that strict polynomial functor theory is unknown.',['Roby1963','FriedlanderSuslin1997','Hua2026'],'high')
add(50,[45,46,47,48],[85,86],T2+':1292-1303','quand et comment ... une structure à p.d.; structure canonique','For modules, Γ(M) has its canonical divided powers on the positive-degree ideal, and evaluation maps Γ^pΓ^q(M)→Γ^{pq}(M) satisfy the PD iteration identities for q≥1. For a general abstract tensor-PD category, existence of such a PD structure is asked, not proved. Graded/topos examples additionally require the relevant symmetry and local sheaf construction.','open on the pages','outputs/recompute.json PD_iteration/binomial_counterexamples; proof_audit.md §6 checks the rank-one coefficient3 at p=q=2 and obstruction to PD on the unit ideal of Z.','C','Search S137-07/08: Stacks07GL states the PD axioms, including iteration; Roby/SGA4 give the module model. The reverse PD evaluation is not inverse to α. No exact arbitrary-category PD theorem under the page’s abbreviated axioms was located.','Roby1963; SGA4 1973; contemporary Stacks definition checked2026.','Canonical positive-ideal module case established; abstract existence and graded symmetry conventions remain to be specified.',['Roby1963','SGA4XVII','StacksPD'],'high')
add(51,[49,95],[86],T2+':1304-1310','non seulement comme application ensembliste; Γ^p ... polynomiale','Composition is sought as a polynomial law in the inner Hom module, linear in the outer one, or equivalently as compatible degree-p polynomial-law structure on f↦Γ^p(f). The usual module case has this law over all base algebras; a set-valued functor alone is insufficient for an arbitrary tensor category.','open on the pages','proof_audit.md §6 distinguishes laws from finite-field functions and preserves composition direction.','C','Search S137-07/08/13: Roby1963 laws and Friedlander–Suslin1997 §2 Definition2.1 supply explicit structured examples, the latter for finite-dimensional vector spaces over a field. These hypotheses do not automatically cover arbitrary k-additive tensor categories or ringed topoi.','Roby1963; Friedlander–Suslin1997.','Module/fixed-field strict-polynomial versions established; exact general enrichment request remains conditional.',['Roby1963','FriedlanderSuslin1997','SGA4XVII'],'high')
add(52,[],[3,5],T1+':44-79;134-174','APPENDIX H — The Hirsch Method; Riemannian model','Embedded printed English source, not a theorem authored on these handwritten pages: Hirsch differential-algebra models for principal bundles/Postnikov constructions, and a Riemannian/Jacobian/Hodge discussion. The author-hosted Sullivan typescript matches these pages verbatim at its printed112 and105, respectively.','stated without proof','No new computation of this externally printed material; provenance checked by PDF screenshots. This record preserves its inclusion in the folder without assigning authorship to Grothendieck.','E','Search S137-04/06: Sullivan’s author bibliography item17 links the matching typescript under Differential forms and the topology of manifolds (1975). The hosted typescript’s printed87-139 differs from the cited published37-49 pagination; exact edition remains uncertain. Sullivan1977 §§7-10 supplies the later rational framework.','Author bibliography labels1975 publication of Tokyo1973 proceedings; hosted typescript version not independently dated.','Identified as Sullivan source material; its full hypotheses must be read in that source, and it is excluded from Grothendieck-original theorem counts.',['SullivanTypescript1975','SullivanBibliography','Sullivan1977'],'high')
